WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.320 --> 00:00:04.860
Would a mega-murderous, universe-killing snap
by any other name sound as harsh?

00:00:04.860 --> 00:00:08.260
After the shocking events that played out
in the final moments of Avengers: Infinity

00:00:08.260 --> 00:00:12.259
War - you know, when Thanos powered up the
Infinity Gauntlet, then snapped his fingers

00:00:12.259 --> 00:00:16.700
and wiped out half of all living creatures
across every galaxy in existence - Marvel

00:00:16.700 --> 00:00:20.810
fans have been at a loss as to what to call
the Mad Titan's horrifying act.

00:00:20.810 --> 00:00:25.240
While most people have referred to it as "the
Snap" or by the more creative name "the Snappening,"

00:00:25.240 --> 00:00:28.769
Thanos is the only character who's bothered
to try to give it a name.

00:00:28.769 --> 00:00:34.629
"With all six stones I could simply snap my
fingers and they would all cease to exist,

00:00:34.629 --> 00:00:37.649
and I call that mercy."

00:00:37.649 --> 00:00:41.620
Unless you're a genocidal monster, though,
that's not the best name to use for it.

00:00:41.620 --> 00:00:45.300
For their part, not even Marvel has given
the moment a legitimate moniker.

00:00:45.300 --> 00:00:46.720
That is, until now.

00:00:46.720 --> 00:00:50.879
Thanks to the publication of the most recent
Avengers: Infinity War tie-in novel, The Cosmic

00:00:50.879 --> 00:00:56.059
Quest Volume Two: Aftermath by Brandon T.
Snider, Thanos' snap has an official name

00:00:56.059 --> 00:00:58.239
- and it's a brutal one.

00:00:58.239 --> 00:01:02.140
To those who survived being snapped out of
existence by the Mad Titan, the act is known

00:01:02.140 --> 00:01:03.450
as "the Decimation."

00:01:03.450 --> 00:01:07.160
While the Avengers and company clearly know
all the heartbreaking circumstances that surround

00:01:07.160 --> 00:01:11.530
the moment - the vigilantes joining forces
in battles across the globe, several heroes

00:01:11.530 --> 00:01:17.450
making incredible sacrifices, and many crumbling
away to dust, some in each other's arms - non-superpowered

00:01:17.450 --> 00:01:20.180
humans spared by the Decimation won't know
the truth.

00:01:20.180 --> 00:01:22.650
"Wait, wh - where'd everybody go?"

00:01:22.650 --> 00:01:26.490
In The Cosmic Quest Volume Two: Aftermath,
the Avengers have concealed the truth from

00:01:26.490 --> 00:01:30.770
the rest of humanity, believing that revealing
the fact that Thanos was responsible for taking

00:01:30.770 --> 00:01:34.119
the lives of billions of people would "hardly
help the world to heal."

00:01:34.119 --> 00:01:37.840
No one but Earth's Mightiest Heroes and the
band of Marvel vigilantes involved with the

00:01:37.840 --> 00:01:40.220
event know what actually happened.

00:01:40.220 --> 00:01:44.479
Everyone else is only aware that most people
in the world have vanished without a trace,

00:01:44.480 --> 00:01:46.900
and aren't aware of the reason why.

00:01:46.900 --> 00:01:49.160
"Something's happening.”

00:01:55.900 --> 00:01:59.560
For comic book fans, the name "the Decimation"
should ring a big bell.

00:01:59.560 --> 00:02:03.820
In the Marvel source material, the moniker
was previously employed to refer to the aftermath

00:02:03.820 --> 00:02:07.751
of the event that happened in the "House of
M" storyline, which featured Scarlet Witch

00:02:07.751 --> 00:02:10.840
stripping powers from 90 percent of the world's
mutants.

00:02:10.840 --> 00:02:14.520
The "depowered mutants" suffered terrible
fates after Scarlet Witch wiped away their

00:02:14.520 --> 00:02:18.920
abilities, with some fading away and eventually
dying without their powers.

00:02:18.920 --> 00:02:23.000
Though it's fitting that The Cosmic Quest
Volume Two: Aftermath would pluck "the Decimation"

00:02:23.000 --> 00:02:27.130
name from the Marvel comic canon given its
similarity to the aftermath of the "House

00:02:27.130 --> 00:02:31.550
of M" event, it remains to be seen whether
Marvel Studios and directors Joe and Anthony

00:02:31.550 --> 00:02:36.270
Russo will implement the name in Avengers
4, or if the heroes will, as they have done

00:02:36.270 --> 00:02:40.690
in the comics and this new companion novel,
keep Thanos' snap a secret from humans.

00:02:40.690 --> 00:02:45.090
Thanos' snap and Scarlet Witch's power-clearing
in the House of M storyline are incredibly

00:02:45.090 --> 00:02:49.200
similar to one another, and it makes total
sense why the heroes who made it out alive

00:02:49.200 --> 00:02:52.510
would want to save others from the trauma
of the full story.

00:02:52.510 --> 00:02:56.110
But will fans hear that name and witness that
secret-keeping in Avengers 4?

00:02:56.110 --> 00:02:59.830
We don't feel like we're reaching in saying
that it's possible, but knowing Marvel, anything

00:02:59.830 --> 00:03:01.040
can happen.

00:03:01.040 --> 00:03:05.160
Marvel has a tendency to keep any and all
Avengers-related details in near-impenetrable

00:03:05.160 --> 00:03:10.440
lockboxes, so to make any confident declarations
about the contents of Avengers 4 would be

00:03:10.440 --> 00:03:11.440
silly.

00:03:11.440 --> 00:03:15.700
At the end of the day, fans can find out what
Thanos' snap will be called in Avengers 4

00:03:15.700 --> 00:03:18.380
when the film opens in theaters on May 3,
2019.

